# CRSNR Analysis

This directory provides the code for the Cumulative Relative Signal-to-Noise Ratio (CRSNR) analysis presented in the paper.

The analysis is used to investigate the cumulative contribution of cyclic-frequency components and the variation of CRSNR with the cyclic-frequency range.

## Data Preparation

The noise samples N1–N6 are selected from the natural noise samples in the ShipsEar dataset. The remaining samples are collected from the ShipsEar and DeepShip datasets.

All audio samples are downsampled to 16 kHz.

For the time-frequency representation, a frame length of 50 ms × 16 kHz and a frame shift of 25 ms × 16 kHz are used. Therefore, the resulting spectrogram can be regarded as being sampled along the time axis with a period of 25 ms.

Accordingly, the maximum cyclic frequency considered in the CRSNR analysis is

amax=0.5 * (1 / 25ms) = 20 Hz

## Usage

Run the following script directly:

```bash
python avg_CRSNR.py